# Modern Icon Protocol

Always use modern icon libraries throughout the website for a cohesive, state-of-the-art aesthetic.

## Allowed

- **`lucide-react`** — standard UI icons (buttons, navigation, status, badges, avatars)
- **`@lordicon/react`** / `LordIconWrapper` — animated premium icons for hero/feature spots
- **`MoonPhaseIcon`** from `components/icons/modernIcons.tsx` — lunar calendar phases only

## Prohibited in UI

- Emoji as icons (`🙏`, `📜`, `✨`, etc.)
- FontAwesome, Glyphicons, Material Icons, or ad-hoc inline SVG duplicates
- Unicode symbols where a Lucide equivalent exists (`✓`, `✡`, `◆`)

## Implementation

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
{ icon: '🙏' }
<span>📜 Explore Scripture</span>

// ✅ GOOD
import { HandHeart, ScrollText } from 'lucide-react';
{ Icon: HandHeart }
<ScrollText size={16} className="text-[#D4AF37]" />
```

## Styling

- Size with `size={n}` prop or Tailwind `w-* h-*`
- Match brand colors via `className` (e.g. `text-[#D4AF37]`)
- Use consistent sizing: 14px chips, 16px buttons, 20–24px section headers

## Exceptions

- AI response text content (markdown from LLM) may contain emojis
- Console logs and admin-only string notices are exempt
